GR: Title I, Book III of the Labor Code dealing with hours of work, weekly rest periods, holidays, service incentive leaves and service charges, covers all employees in ALL establishments 
XPNS: 
1.	Government employees or any of its political subdivision and goccs with original charters
2.	Managerial employees and members of the managerial staff 
o	Primary duty consists of the management of the establishment in which they are employed or of a department or subdivision 
o	They exercise independent judgment and discretion  

Members of the managerial staff (supervisory employees)  
	Exempted from the coverage if the following are their duties: 
a.	Primary duty - consists in the performance of work directly related to management policies of their employer 
b.	Customarily and regularly exercise discretion and independent judgment  
c.	Regularly and directly assist a (management of the proprietor establishment) execute under general supervision, work along specialized or technical lines requiring special training. 
d.	They do not devote more than 20% of their hours worked in a workweek to activities which are not directly and closely related to the performance of the work described above  
Test of Supervisory or Managerial Status 
depends on whether a person possesses authority that is not merely routinary or clerical in nature but one that requires use of independent judgment 
3.	Field personnel - Refer to non-agricultural employees who regularly perform their duties away from the principal place of business or branch office of the employer and whose actual hours of work in the field cannot be determined with reasonable certainty  
a.	Non-agricultural employees who regularly perform their duties away from the principal place of business or branch office of the er 
b.	and whose actual hours of work in the field cannot be determined with reasonable certainty
4.	Members of the family of employer who are dependent upon him for chief support 
a.	Exempted from the coverage, for the support given by the employer may exceed the benefit for which an employee is entitled under appropriate labor provisions. 
b.	Evil sought to be prevented- may create labor problems that would break up the family
5.	Domestic helpers 
a.	Those in the personal service of another 
b.	Employer's home 
c.	Usually necessary desirable for the maintenance and enjoyment thereof 
d.	Minister to the personal comfort, convenience, or safety of the employer as well as members of his households 
e.	Employment of house helper in commercial, industrial and agricultural enterprises entitles them to salary and benefits provided under the labor code
6.	Workers paid by result 
a.	On piece rates or task basis - Task basis-payment if on the completion of the work 
b.	Compensation is based on the work completed and not on the time spent in working 
c.	Unsupervised-pakyao and takay basis 
d.	Piece rate- garment factories - work is done in employer's premises 
e.	Pakyao an takay - in agricultural industry-work is performed in bulk or in volumes which is difficult to quantify  
